			<item>
				<title>Table-Driven Tests</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/table/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/table/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;table-driven-tests&#34;&gt;Table-Driven Tests&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#table-driven-tests&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You&amp;rsquo;ve &lt;em&gt;run&lt;/em&gt; dozens of table tests by now. This is the exercise where you&#xA;learn to &lt;em&gt;read&lt;/em&gt; one as a design — because from here on, every test you&#xA;write yourself will wear this shape.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-pattern-named&#34;&gt;The pattern, named&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#the-pattern-named&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-go&#34; data-lang=&#34;go&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;TestGrade&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tests&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; []&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;struct&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;score&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;int&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt;  &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;string&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        {&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;95&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;A&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;},&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        {&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;85&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;B&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;},&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        {&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;75&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;C&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;},&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        {&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;59&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;F&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;},&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tt&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;range&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tests&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Grade&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Errorf&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Grade(%d) = %q, want %q&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;score&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;tt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Table, loop, verdict. The table lists input/output pairs as data — adding&#xA;a case means adding a line, never a function. The loop runs every row. The&#xA;verdict compares and reports. Three moving parts, endless reuse: this one&#xA;shape covers the overwhelming majority of Go unit tests in the wild.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Subtests</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/subtests/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/subtests/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;subtests&#34;&gt;Subtests&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#subtests&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tables collect rows; subtests give them &lt;em&gt;names&lt;/em&gt;. When &lt;code&gt;TestGrade&lt;/code&gt; fails you&#xA;learn a score mismatched — but which scenario? Above? Below? The boundary&#xA;itself? &lt;code&gt;t.Run&lt;/code&gt; splits one test into labeled children, and each child&#xA;reports, passes, and filters independently.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;naming-the-cases&#34;&gt;Naming the cases&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#naming-the-cases&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-go&#34; data-lang=&#34;go&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;TestClamp&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Run&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;above&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Clamp&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;99&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;), &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Fatalf&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Clamp(99, 0, 10) = %d, want %d&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    })&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Run&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;below&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    })&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Run&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;inside&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// ...&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    })&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;t.Run(&amp;quot;above&amp;quot;, func(t *testing.T) {...})&lt;/code&gt; registers a child test carrying&#xA;its own &lt;code&gt;*testing.T&lt;/code&gt;. Failures name the child — &lt;code&gt;TestClamp/below&lt;/code&gt; — so the&#xA;output points at the broken &lt;em&gt;scenario&lt;/em&gt;, not just the broken function. With&#xA;&lt;code&gt;-v&lt;/code&gt;, every subtest gets its own line, PASS or FAIL; a table&amp;rsquo;s rows, by&#xA;contrast, all hide inside one verdict.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Test Helpers</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/helpers/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/helpers/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;test-helpers&#34;&gt;Test Helpers&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#test-helpers&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The third time you type the same assertion, stop. Extract it — into a&#xA;helper function that takes &lt;code&gt;t&lt;/code&gt; and does the checking. But helpers create a&#xA;new problem: when one fails, &lt;em&gt;whose line&lt;/em&gt; does the failure point at? This&#xA;exercise&amp;rsquo;s test calls the answer before you write a line of your own.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;infrastructure-wears-a-mark&#34;&gt;Infrastructure wears a mark&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#infrastructure-wears-a-mark&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-go&#34; data-lang=&#34;go&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;mustMean&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt; []&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;float64&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;float64&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Helper&lt;/span&gt;()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Mean&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt;); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Fatalf&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Mean(%v) = %v, want %v&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;xs&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;want&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;t.Helper()&lt;/code&gt; as the first line marks the function as scaffolding. When the&#xA;&lt;code&gt;Fatalf&lt;/code&gt; inside fires, Go skips helper frames and reports the &lt;em&gt;caller&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/em&gt;&#xA;line — the &lt;code&gt;mustMean(t, ...)&lt;/code&gt; invocation in the test, with its specific&#xA;input. Without that call, every failure would point inside the helper at&#xA;the same &lt;code&gt;t.Fatalf&lt;/code&gt; line, and you&amp;rsquo;d guess which input broke. One line of&#xA;marking, failures that locate themselves.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Testdata Fixtures</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/testdata/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/testdata/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;testdata-fixtures&#34;&gt;Testdata Fixtures&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#testdata-fixtures&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tests that read files need files to read — checked in, versioned, and&#xA;sitting where the test expects them. Go&amp;rsquo;s answer is a directory named&#xA;&lt;code&gt;testdata/&lt;/code&gt;, and the name is a contract with the toolchain, not a&#xA;suggestion.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-directory-the-build-ignores&#34;&gt;The directory the build ignores&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#the-directory-the-build-ignores&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Any directory called &lt;code&gt;testdata&lt;/code&gt; is skipped by the Go tool: &lt;code&gt;go build&lt;/code&gt;&#xA;won&amp;rsquo;t compile packages inside it, &lt;code&gt;go vet&lt;/code&gt; looks past it. That makes it&#xA;the standard home for everything tests consume but programs never import —&#xA;sample inputs, golden outputs, and in this exercise, a small poem:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Example Tests</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/examples/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/examples/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;example-tests&#34;&gt;Example Tests&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#example-tests&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Documentation rots. Every prose claim about what code does — &amp;ldquo;returns twice&#xA;its input&amp;rdquo; — decays the moment the code changes and nobody updates the&#xA;sentence. Unless the sentence &lt;em&gt;runs&lt;/em&gt;. This exercise&amp;rsquo;s test file contains no&#xA;&lt;code&gt;Test&lt;/code&gt; function at all, yet &lt;code&gt;go test&lt;/code&gt; verifies it. Here&amp;rsquo;s how.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;documentation-that-executes&#34;&gt;Documentation that executes&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#documentation-that-executes&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-go&#34; data-lang=&#34;go&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;ExampleDouble&lt;/span&gt;() {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;fmt&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Println&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Double&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;))&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#75715e&#34;&gt;// Output: 4&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A function named &lt;code&gt;ExampleDouble&lt;/code&gt; is two things at once. To &lt;code&gt;godoc&lt;/code&gt; it&amp;rsquo;s&#xA;documentation, rendered beside the package&amp;rsquo;s reference page as a runnable&#xA;illustration. To &lt;code&gt;go test&lt;/code&gt; it&amp;rsquo;s a test: the body executes, stdout is&#xA;captured, and the capture is compared against the &lt;code&gt;// Output:&lt;/code&gt; comment&#xA;&lt;em&gt;line by line, byte for byte&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Benchmarks</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/benchmarks/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/benchmarks/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;benchmarks&#34;&gt;Benchmarks&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#benchmarks&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tests answer &amp;ldquo;does it work?&amp;rdquo; Benchmarks answer &amp;ldquo;how fast?&amp;rdquo; — and Go keeps&#xA;the two side by side in the same file, sharing helpers and fixtures. This&#xA;exercise&amp;rsquo;s package holds both: &lt;code&gt;TestFib&lt;/code&gt; guards correctness while&#xA;&lt;code&gt;BenchmarkFib&lt;/code&gt; times it, and a third test guards the benchmark itself.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;measuring-not-asserting&#34;&gt;Measuring, not asserting&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#measuring-not-asserting&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-go&#34; data-lang=&#34;go&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;BenchmarkFib&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;b&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;B&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;i&lt;/span&gt; &amp;lt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;b&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;N&lt;/span&gt;; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;i&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;++&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Fib&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;BenchmarkXxx&lt;/code&gt; takes &lt;code&gt;*testing.B&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;b.N&lt;/code&gt; is the runner&amp;rsquo;s dial: it calls&#xA;your function with growing &lt;code&gt;N&lt;/code&gt; until timings stabilize, then reports&#xA;nanoseconds per operation. You don&amp;rsquo;t choose the iteration count — the&#xA;harness calibrates it. Your only job is putting the operation inside the&#xA;loop, exactly once per iteration, with setup hoisted outside.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Asserting Errors</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/errassert/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/100-exercises-to-learn-go/08_testing/errassert/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;asserting-errors&#34;&gt;Asserting Errors&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#asserting-errors&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The calculator section divided two ways: &lt;code&gt;Divide&lt;/code&gt; that &lt;em&gt;panics&lt;/em&gt; on zero,&#xA;and — implicitly — the question of what the alternative looks like. Here&#xA;it is. Same function name, same arithmetic, opposite philosophy: failure&#xA;as a return value the caller must confront, not an explosion it might&#xA;survive.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;both-branches-or-it-isnt-tested&#34;&gt;Both branches, or it isn&amp;rsquo;t tested&lt;a class=&#34;anchor&#34; href=&#34;#both-branches-or-it-isnt-tested&#34;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-go&#34; data-lang=&#34;go&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;func&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;TestDivide&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;testing&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;T&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Divide&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;6&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;3&lt;/span&gt;); &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;||&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Fatalf&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Divide(6, 3) = (%d, %v), want (2, nil)&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;got&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;_&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;err&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;:=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Divide&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;); !&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;errors&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Is&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;ErrZeroDivisor&lt;/span&gt;) {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;t&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;Fatalf&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;Divide(1, 0) err = %v, want ErrZeroDivisor&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;err&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    }&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Error-returning functions have two contracts, and the test pins both. The&#xA;happy path asserts &lt;em&gt;two facts&lt;/em&gt;: the value is right &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; the error is&#xA;&lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt; — checking only the quotient would pass a function that divides&#xA;correctly while crying wolf. The failure path asserts identity via&#xA;&lt;code&gt;errors.Is&lt;/code&gt;, never &lt;code&gt;==&lt;/code&gt;: a wrapped &lt;code&gt;ErrZeroDivisor&lt;/code&gt; with context attached&#xA;represents the same problem, and &lt;code&gt;==&lt;/code&gt; would blind the test to it. The&#xA;sentinel lesson&amp;rsquo;s rule, enforced at the assertion site.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
